     "text": [
      "==================================================================\n",
      "FROM THE SIMULATION\n",
      "  fitted plateau density            1.639 g/cm3\n",
      "  molar mass (from the xyz)        577.92 g/mol\n",
      "  volume per molecule               585.7 A^3\n",
      "  SLAB_THICK                        14.37 A   (area)\n",
      "  L_MOL x LAT_FRAC                  14.28 A   (aspect ratio)\n",
      "  PI_STACK                           3.40 A\n",
      "  median gamma                       70.4 deg\n",
      "  bulk cell area = V/SLAB_THICK     40.76 A^2\n",
      "\n",
      "  depth-weighted lattice (rho x Debye-Waller over the fitted profile)\n",
      "    lamellar (out-of-plane)   d =  12.08 A   q = 0.522 +/- 0.031\n",
      "    column   (in-plane)       d =   3.58 A   q = 1.821 +/- 0.264\n",
      "\n",
      "MEASURED (pseudo-Voigt on a local background)\n",
      "  out-of-plane order 1   q = 0.4997 +/- 0.0003   d = 12.574 A   FWHM = 0.0579   q_n/q_1 = 1.000\n",
      "  out-of-plane order 2   q = 0.9982 +/- 0.0059   d =  6.294 A   FWHM = 0.1207   q_n/q_1 = 1.998\n",
      "  out-of-plane order 3   q = 1.4968 +/- 0.0588   d =  4.198 A   FWHM = 0.2355   q_n/q_1 = 2.995\n",
      "  in-plane pi stack     q = 1.8873 +/- 0.0022   d =  3.329 A   FWHM = 0.3685\n",
      "\n",
      "MEASURED vs MODEL\n",
      "  (200) out-of-plane  q  0.500 /  0.522   d  12.57 /  12.08    -4.0%\n",
      "  (pi-pi) in-plane    q  1.887 /  1.821   d   3.33 /   3.58    +7.6%\n",
      "  cell area           d_lam x d_pi  41.86 /  43.26    +3.3%\n",
      "\n",
      "IMPLIED KNOBS (from the out-of-plane / pi-pi pair)\n",
      "  SLAB_THICK       =   13.99 A   (now 14.37)\n",
      "  L_MOL x LAT_FRAC =   14.46 A   (now 14.28)\n",
      "    L_MOL and LAT_FRAC are exactly degenerate, only the product matters:\n",
      "      L_MOL = 13.18  ->  LAT_FRAC = 1.097\n",
      "      L_MOL = 13.60  ->  LAT_FRAC = 1.063\n",
      "      L_MOL = 14.95  ->  LAT_FRAC = 0.967\n",
      "\n",
      "UNIT CELL (all three measured peaks + the fitted density)\n",
      "                   this film  alpha-ZnPc    diff\n",
      "  a (A)                29.12       25.92    +12%\n",
      "  b (A)                 3.33        3.79    -12%\n",
      "  c (A)                27.98       23.92    +17%\n",
      "  beta (deg)          120.28      121.60     -1%\n",
      "  density               1.64        1.92    -15%\n",
      "\n",
      "  CAUTION. beta lands close to the literature value, but a, b and c\n",
      "  are off by more than 10%, so the beta agreement alone is not evidence\n",
      "  the assignment is right. Treat it as a consistency figure only.\n",
      "==================================================================\n"
     ]
