     "text": [
      "========================================================================\n",
      "GROUND TRUTH, nothing here is adjustable\n",
      "  molar mass (xyz stoichiometry)        577.92 g/mol\n",
      "  plateau density (fit)                  1.639 g/cm3\n",
      "  volume per molecule                    585.7 A^3\n",
      "  median gamma (fit)                      70.4 deg\n",
      "  rho(z), gamma(z)                     the fitted profiles\n",
      "\n",
      "BOUNDED BY THE XYZ GEOMETRY\n",
      "  heavy-atom span                        13.18 A\n",
      "  hydrogen-inclusive span                14.95 A\n",
      "  vdW envelope diameter                  13.76 to 14.53 A\n",
      "  vdW thickness                           3.59 A\n",
      "    L_MOL      now  14.95, must lie in this diameter window\n",
      "    SLAB_THICK now  14.37, same window, it is the same width\n",
      "    PI_STACK   now   3.40, at or below the vdW thickness; the\n",
      "               measured column spacing is 3.33 A\n",
      "\n",
      "FREE, and what each one moves\n",
      "  LAT_FRAC                 the only genuine shape knob, 0 < LAT_FRAC <= 1\n",
      "  STRAIN_MIN / STRAIN_MAX  clamp on the density-driven area, bites at the\n",
      "                           surface and sets how far the bands spread\n",
      "  STRAIN_ANISO_SI          splits the spread between the two directions\n",
      "  POS_DISORDER_VAC / _SI   Debye-Waller weight, moves the depth average\n",
      "                           without moving any spacing\n",
      "  splay, glide, libration, seed        drawing only, no lattice effect\n",
      "\n",
      "REDUNDANCY. Only L_MOL * LAT_FRAC / PI_STACK enters the aspect ratio, so\n",
      "one of the three is redundant. Locking L_MOL to the xyz and PI_STACK to\n",
      "the measured column spacing leaves LAT_FRAC as the single free number.\n",
      "\n",
      "WHERE THE TWO MEASURED PEAKS PUT THE KNOBS\n",
      "  current   SLAB_THICK  14.37   L_MOL x LAT_FRAC  14.28   ->  d_lam  12.08  d_pi  3.58\n",
      "  crossing  SLAB_THICK  15.03   L_MOL x LAT_FRAC  16.19   ->  LAT_FRAC 1.083 at L_MOL = 14.95\n",
      "  algebraic SLAB_THICK  13.99   (volume per molecule divided by the measured cell area)\n",
      "\n",
      "INTERNAL CONSISTENCY\n",
      "  the column period is the pi-pi contact, so d_pi should equal PI_STACK.\n",
      "  model d_pi 3.58 A against PI_STACK 3.40 A, +5.4%. Nothing in the module enforces this;\n",
      "  imposing it would remove the last free knob rather than add one.\n",
      "========================================================================\n"
     ]
